WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.267
-Today is Friday,
and that's usually when

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:03.734
I catch up on some
personal stuff.

00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:05.834
You know, I check my inbox,
I return some e-mails,

00:00:05.834 --> 00:00:08.000
and of course, I send out
thank you notes,

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.467
and I was running a bit behind.

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:11.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.234 --> 00:00:13.601
Thanks for letting me
write some notes tonight.

00:00:13.601 --> 00:00:15.968
James, can I get some thank you
note writing music, please?

00:00:15.968 --> 00:00:17.634
[ Gentle music plays ]

00:00:17.634 --> 00:00:20.000
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.167
♪♪

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:25.033
-Is he okay?
-Great mood tonight.

00:00:25.033 --> 00:00:28.667
-Yeah, wow.
-Here we go. [ Clears throat ]

00:00:28.667 --> 00:00:29.801
[ Gentle music plays ]

00:00:29.801 --> 00:00:31.801
Thank you, hay rides,

00:00:31.801 --> 00:00:33.534
for giving kids the chance
to experience

00:00:33.534 --> 00:00:35.601
how fun it is to be hay.

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:37.834
[ Applause ]

00:00:38.567 --> 00:00:40.501
Go on rides all the time.
-Come on.

00:00:40.501 --> 00:00:42.033
-It's cool, man.
-Be-hay-ve.

00:00:42.033 --> 00:00:44.734
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.467 --> 00:00:47.167
-Hayyy.

00:00:47.167 --> 00:00:49.000
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.501
[ Gentle music plays ]

00:00:50.501 --> 00:00:54.200
Thank you, answering someone's
texts with a thumbs up,

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.634
for saying, "this is where
the conversation ends."

00:00:56.634 --> 00:00:59.167
[ Applause ]

00:01:03.534 --> 00:01:06.133
We're good.
Yeah, yeah. Sure, sure.

00:01:06.133 --> 00:01:07.834
-Thumbs up.
-We're good.

00:01:09.634 --> 00:01:10.968
[ Gentle music plays ]

00:01:10.968 --> 00:01:13.067
Thank you, apple picking,

00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:15.267
for somehow costing
five times more

00:01:15.267 --> 00:01:17.434
than when someone else
does it for you.

00:01:17.434 --> 00:01:19.434
[ Applause ]

00:01:19.801 --> 00:01:21.667
I picked these.

00:01:23.267 --> 00:01:26.000
I picked these!

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.100
They're 20 times more than I
would normally buy at the store.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:31.734
-At Whole Foods, too.
-Yeah, man.

00:01:31.734 --> 00:01:33.901
-$300 for an apple?

00:01:33.901 --> 00:01:35.934
Pretty steep.

00:01:35.934 --> 00:01:37.334
[ Gentle music plays ]

00:01:37.334 --> 00:01:39.167
-Thank you, matchsticks,

00:01:39.167 --> 00:01:41.534
for being toothpicks that
got their nails done.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:43.200
Oh!

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.734
[ Applause ]
Good.

00:01:47.634 --> 00:01:49.434
-That's a cute one.

00:01:49.434 --> 00:01:51.434
[ Audience member laughs ]

00:01:51.434 --> 00:01:52.934
[ Gentle music plays ]

00:01:52.934 --> 00:01:54.734
-That's a good laugh.
-Yeah.

00:01:54.734 --> 00:01:56.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:57.801
That's a great laugh, yeah.

00:01:57.801 --> 00:02:00.167
-That's beautiful.
-It's a good laughing crowd.

00:02:00.167 --> 00:02:02.567
I love this crowd.

00:02:02.567 --> 00:02:03.868
-It's a good Friday crowd.
-What's that?

00:02:03.868 --> 00:02:07.133
Don't ruin it.
We're having a good thing.

00:02:07.133 --> 00:02:10.367
[ Applause ]

00:02:10.367 --> 00:02:11.701
-I didn't hear you.
What'd you say?

00:02:11.701 --> 00:02:13.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:17.667
-I said New York City is
the best city in the world!

00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:19.734
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's what I said!

00:02:22.767 --> 00:02:24.467
Alright, here we go.

00:02:24.467 --> 00:02:25.667
[ Gentle music plays ]

00:02:25.667 --> 00:02:28.701
Thank you, chicken nuggets
and fish sticks,

00:02:28.701 --> 00:02:30.167
for not making it awkward
when you

00:02:30.167 --> 00:02:31.767
showed up to the party
in the same outfit.

00:02:31.767 --> 00:02:32.934
It's like, oh!

00:02:32.934 --> 00:02:35.334
[ Applause ]

00:02:35.334 --> 00:02:37.067
Really?

00:02:38.534 --> 00:02:40.033
[ Gentle music plays ]

00:02:40.033 --> 00:02:42.133
Thank you, leaf blowers,

00:02:42.133 --> 00:02:43.534
for being there whenever
I want to

00:02:43.534 --> 00:02:45.367
make my problem
someone else's problem.

00:02:45.367 --> 00:02:47.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:48.734
[ Applause ]

00:02:51.267 --> 00:02:53.667
"How you doing, Dave?"

00:02:53.667 --> 00:02:55.100
-"6:00 in the morning, Dave."

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:56.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.567 --> 00:02:58.133
-"This is gas-powered, too.

00:02:58.133 --> 00:02:59.467
I don't know if you can tell."

00:02:59.467 --> 00:03:02.100
[ Imitates leaf blower ]

00:03:02.767 --> 00:03:04.601
"Took the engine from
my son's dirt bike

00:03:04.601 --> 00:03:06.100
and put it on the leaf blower."

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:08.834
-"Took off the muffler
to give it more torque."

00:03:08.834 --> 00:03:11.834
-"I took off the muffler.
It just sounds cooler."

00:03:11.834 --> 00:03:13.567
-[ Imitates leaf blower ]
-[ Imitates leaf blower ]

00:03:14.334 --> 00:03:16.634
-"Hey, good morning, Dave.
Appreciate ya."

00:03:18.367 --> 00:03:19.734
"Might want to step on
that paper bag

00:03:19.734 --> 00:03:21.234
that's on fire on
your front porch."

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:23.033
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.033 --> 00:03:24.868
-"Put some sugar in
your gas tank, Dave.

00:03:24.868 --> 00:03:26.634
Flat tires."

00:03:26.634 --> 00:03:28.767
-"Dave, why don't you come over?
I want to give you a wedgie.

00:03:28.767 --> 00:03:30.801
Come on, just turn around.

00:03:30.801 --> 00:03:32.000
Alright, buddy.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:33.400
Best neighbor ever."

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:35.634
-"3:00 in the morning, Dave!"

00:03:35.634 --> 00:03:37.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.767 --> 00:03:39.734
-"It's 3:00 in the morning
somewhere, Dave!"

00:03:39.734 --> 00:03:41.701
-[ Imitates leaf blower ]

00:03:43.801 --> 00:03:46.801
[ Imitates leaf blower revving ]

00:03:49.501 --> 00:03:51.100
-For blowing leaves?
-Yeah.

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:54.133
-Wow. Wow.
-Took his son's dirt bike.

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:55.767
So now his kid doesn't even
have a dirt bike.

00:03:55.767 --> 00:03:57.968
-"He doesn't even need
to ride it, Dave.

00:03:57.968 --> 00:03:59.667
He's having enough fun
on the internet,

00:03:59.667 --> 00:04:01.133
playing robots or whatever.

00:04:01.133 --> 00:04:02.267
Check this thing out."

00:04:02.267 --> 00:04:04.701
[ Imitates leaf blower revving ]

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:08.200
-"Got a new chainsaw!"

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:10.634
[ Imitates chainsaw revving ]

00:04:10.634 --> 00:04:12.067
[ Imitates leaf blower revving ]

00:04:12.067 --> 00:04:13.834
[ Imitates chainsaw revving ]

00:04:18.334 --> 00:04:20.133
[ Gentle music playing ]

00:04:20.133 --> 00:04:22.767
Thank you, electrical outlets,

00:04:22.767 --> 00:04:24.267
for being wall nostrils.

00:04:24.267 --> 00:04:26.567
[ Applause ]

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:32.000
[ Chuckles ]

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.267
[ Gentle music playing ]

00:04:33.267 --> 00:04:35.534
Thank you, cinnamon sticks,

00:04:35.534 --> 00:04:37.667
for looking like you'd be
delivered by a raven

00:04:37.667 --> 00:04:39.434
with news from the North.

00:04:39.434 --> 00:04:41.200
[ Applause ]

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:43.267
"Mr. Fallon!"

00:04:43.267 --> 00:04:44.467
[ Applause ]

00:04:44.467 --> 00:04:47.634
-The tea!
-Spice the cider!

